  "problem": "Compute the following:\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(-7)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-34 \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-34 \\\\ 5\\cdot 4+8\\cdot (-2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-34 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-34 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
